'''Alderaanian consular security''', with [[Rebel trooper]]s known as '''Alderaanian Fleet Troopers''' or simply '''Fleet Troopers''' appearing the same,<ref name="FFG Legion Fleet Troopers" /> was the [[Law enforcement agency|security force]] present on [[Alderaan]] and on its [[Starship|consular vessels]], responsible for guarding and escorting [[senator]]s and other dignitaries. When the [[Viceroy]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] became a leading member in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], these forces also played a part in [[Galactic Civil War|fighting]] the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="ROUVG" /><ref name="ANH" />

Due to its simplicity, the consular security uniform was also used as the apparel<ref name="HC 20">{{HelmetCollectionCite|20|Helmets}}</ref> for many [[Rebel trooper]]s<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> after Rebel [[commander]]s recognized the advantages of establishing a standard outfit for the [[Alliance Army]].<ref name="HC 20" /> Amongst the Rebels who used the uniform were those stationed at the [[Great Temple|Rebel headquarters]] on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]]<ref name="ANH" /> and many who fought in the [[operations on Tatooine]].<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> The uniform was still being used by Rebel troopers during the time of the [[Battle of Endor]] and later [[Battle of Theed]], which occurred at a time when the Rebellion was transforming into the [[New Republic]], making its Rebel troopers into [[New Republic soldier]]s.<ref name="Battlefront II" />

==History==
===Battle of Scarif===
{{Quote|Here! Here! Take it! Take it!|An Alderaanian consular security soldier, passing the Death Star plans to Toshma Jefkin|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:FleetTrooper-SWL.png|thumb|left|200px|Many Alderaanian consular security soldiers worked with the Rebel Alliance.]]
By [[1 BBY]],<ref name="RO Date">{{FilmDate|RO}}</ref> many [[Alderaanian]] [[consular]] [[security]] [[soldier]]s were working with the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]],<ref name="Rogue One" /> which also used<ref name="Battlefront II" /> the consular uniform<ref name="ANH" /> for its own [[Rebel trooper]]s.<ref name="Battlefront II" /> Rebels dressed in the uniform worked in the [[Great Temple|main base]] on [[Yavin 4]]. There, they worked as mainly security for the base and its personnel, with one watching [[starship]]s fly in and out on an elevated viewing platform and others attending the meetings with the [[Alliance High Command]]. As well as the ground base, many soldiers were seen on starships such as the [[MC75 Star Cruiser|MC75 star cruiser]] ''[[Profundity]]'' and the [[CR90 corvette]] ''[[Tantive IV]]''.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Among the consular security soldiers on the ground was [[Gale Torg]], who was assigned to [[Security guard|guard]] and escort [[senator]]s and dignitaries who visited the Alliance.<ref name="ROUVG" /> Shortly after a meeting of the High Command, where many consular security personnel were posted, Torg was walking with the former senator [[Mon Mothma]] and [[General]] [[Antoc Merrick]] when [[Private]] [[Tenzigo Weems]], from the [[Rebel Alliance Intelligence Service]], ran to Mothma and Merrick. He told them about a rebel [[Battle of Scarif|attack]] on [[Scarif]] and when they asked of [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] and he claimed he was already on his way there with a large portion of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

Raddus had been notified of the attack by a consular security soldier on the ''Profundity''.<ref name="Rogue One Adaptation 5">[[Rogue One Adaptation 5|''Rogue One Adaptation'' 5]]</ref> His swift response meant he and the Alliance Fleet managed to win at Scarif, although with the cost of the ''Profundity'' being disabled by the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Devastator]]''. Aboard the ''Profundity'', many consular security soldiers were rushing to get onto the ''Tantive IV'', which was docked into the hanger of the [[cruiser]]. However, before making for the ''Tantive IV'', [[Unidentified fleet trooper|one]] of the soldiers stopped at a terminal to extract the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], the very plans they had obtained during the battle, on a [[datacard]]. As he did that, another soldier prompted him to get going and they took the drive and ran down to the next security door. The door malfunctioned and failed to open completely, with the lights turning off simultaneously from the damage made to the ship. After failing to pull it open, the soldier tried to knock for the retreating soldiers on the other side until the twelve trapped men realized there was a sound behind them.<ref name="Rogue One" />

[[File:BattlesthatChangedGalaxy-Vader-boarding.png|thumb|right|350px|Trapped rebel soldiers faced off against Darth Vader and failed to stop him.]]
The dozen consular security soldiers pointed their guns at the darkness until it lit up to show [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] standing before them with his [[Darth Vader's lightsaber|lightsaber]] glowing. The soldiers opened fire and Vader began picking them off. The soldier with the plans continued knocking on the door until [[Toshma Jefkin]] came from the other side of the door to help. As Vader slaughtered the last of the soldiers, Jefkin was given the plans through the gap in the door and he ran into the ''Tantive IV'' as Vader broke through the door, his lightsaber stabbed through the plan's former holder. Jefkin closed the airlock and ordered the corvette to launch. The ''Tantive IV'' descended from the ''Profundity'' and made a quick escape from the system.<ref name="Rogue One" />

===Escorting the Death Star plans===
{{Quote|We intercepted no transmissions! This is a consular ship! We're on a diplomatic mission!|Raymus Antilles, to Darth Vader|<ref name="ANH" />}}
[[File:Reptroops-ANH.png|thumb|left|250px|The Alderaanian consular security soldiers prepare to defend the ''Tantive IV''.]]
Unfortunately, the ''Tantive IV'' was leaking from its [[hyperdrive]] which left a trail for the ''Devastator'' to follow.<ref name="Raymus">{{StoryCite|story=Raymus|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref> [[Captain]] [[Raymus Antilles]] ordered for the consular security soldiers to secure the airlock and prepare the escape pods.<ref name="Rogue One" /> The ''Tantive IV'' [[Secret mission to Tatooine|arrived]] at [[Tatooine]] and was quickly followed by the ''Devastator''<ref name="Raymus" /> which pulled it into its main hanger.<ref name="ANH" /> [[Ensign]] [[Cariso Smadis]]<ref name="Force Collection Cariso">{{ForceCollection|Cariso Smadis|star=2}}</ref> and several other soldiers took position to defend the airlock, where [[stormtrooper]]s blasted their way in, pushing the defenders back. After taking heavy losses, the soldiers were in full retreat, and several were captured. Antilles was captured and interogated by Darth Vader. Antilles denied that they had the Death Star plans and Vader choked him to death in his anger.<ref name="ANH" />

Although the Death Star plans barely escaped the ''Tantive IV'', the Death Star went and destroyed [[Alderaan]] later that day. Soon after, the plans made it to the Alliance's main base, although they were tracked and followed by the Death Star. With the [[battle station]] on its way to destroy Yavin 4, the Alliance swiftly put together an attack that targeted the station's main weakness. With numerous consular security soldiers still present to guard the base, the attack commenced and became a major success, with the Death Star ultimately being destroyed. A large number of consular security soldiers attended the [[Royal Award Ceremony]] that awarded the heroes of the battle.<ref name="ANH" /> These included Captain [[Miara Larte]] and [[Jessamyn]], who were still in mourning for their friends on Alderaan.<ref name="By Whatever Sun">{{StoryCite|story=By Whatever Sun|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref> Gale Torg too was present as well, but as an [[Rebel Honor Guard|Honor Guard]].<ref name="ANH" />

===Legacy===
After the Empire [[Battle of Jakku|fell]], the Alliance transitioned into the [[New Republic]]. The [[New Republic soldier's uniform]] used the same helmet type as the Alderaanian consular security soldiers.<ref name="Chapter 6">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 6: The Prisoner}}</ref>

==Uniforms and equipment==
[[File:ScatterGunTrooper-SWL.png|thumb|right|250px|An Alderaanian consular security soldier using a scatter gun.]]
The troopers of consular security [[Clothing|wore]] pale blue shirts, grey trousers, and black calf length boots. Over the shirts was worn a multi-pocketed black [[spacer]] vest of [[Corellia]]n cut. The [[Alderaanian fleet trooper helmet|distinctive white service helmet]] featured a flash visor as well as, in many cases, an integrated [[comlink]]. They were known to utilize [[DH-17 blaster pistol]]s. [[Officer]]s in consular security wore a similar uniform, but instead sported a light brown jacket, shirt and pants along with a brown belt.<ref name="ROUVG" /><ref name="ANH" />

Many aspects and variants of these uniforms saw service with [[Rebel trooper]]s, especially on [[Yavin 4]]'s [[Great Temple|Base One]].<ref name="ANH" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Alderaanian consular security first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], directed by [[George Lucas]] and released in [[1977]].<ref name="ANH" /> They were later identified as fleet troopers in the game ''Defend the Fleet'' on the [[Fantasy Flight Games]] website.<ref name="FFG Legion Fleet Troopers" /> In [[2016]], the troopers appeared in ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''<ref name="Rogue One" /> and were identified as the Alderaanian consular security in the ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'' that came out simultaneously.<ref name="ROUVG" />

